\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}p dir=\PYGZdq{}ltr\PYGZdq{} style=\PYGZdq{}direction: ltr;text\PYGZhy{}align: justify;line\PYGZhy{}height:200\PYGZpc{};font\PYGZhy{}family:\PYGZsq{}Vazirmatn\PYGZsq{},Tahoma,\PYGZsq{}Segoe UI\PYGZsq{},system\PYGZhy{}ui,Arial,sans\PYGZhy{}serif;font\PYGZhy{}size:medium\PYGZdq{}\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}font size=3\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} The bus across town drops Nika in front of the \PYGZlt{}b\PYGZgt{}Digikala\PYGZlt{}/b\PYGZgt{} tower on a bright Sunday morning, a borrowed badge clipped to her bag and a laptop full of half\PYGZhy{}finished Snapp experiments. Her platform team has lent her out for a two\PYGZhy{}week cross\PYGZhy{}team sprint, because the search group at Digikala wants the same in\PYGZhy{}house language\PYGZhy{}model expertise that Nika has been building since she wrote her first character tokenizer. The problem on the table is deceptively ordinary, namely the little box at the top of the marketplace where millions of people type the first few letters of what they want to buy. Today that box completes a query by matching prefixes, which means it has no idea that the word \PYGZlt{}i\PYGZgt{}case\PYGZlt{}/i\PYGZgt{} after \PYGZlt{}i\PYGZgt{}phone\PYGZlt{}/i\PYGZgt{} means something very different from \PYGZlt{}i\PYGZgt{}case\PYGZlt{}/i\PYGZgt{} after \PYGZlt{}i\PYGZgt{}court\PYGZlt{}/i\PYGZgt{}. The search lead, Sahar, wants completions that read the whole context and not just the last word, and she is convinced the answer is the attention mechanism that powers every modern GPT. Nika has already turned text into clean integer tensors in her previous notebook, so tonight she finally gets to build the part that made Transformers famous. She opens a fresh notebook, pours a glass of tea, and this is exactly where you join her.}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}/font\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}/p\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} }
