\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}h3 style=\PYGZdq{}line\PYGZhy{}height:200\PYGZpc{};font\PYGZhy{}family:\PYGZsq{}Vazirmatn\PYGZsq{},Tahoma,\PYGZsq{}Segoe UI\PYGZsq{},system\PYGZhy{}ui,Arial,sans\PYGZhy{}serif;color:\PYGZsh{}EF4056\PYGZdq{}\PYGZgt{}1. Scaled dot\PYGZhy{}product attention and the causal mask\PYGZlt{}/h3\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}p style=\PYGZdq{}line\PYGZhy{}height:180\PYGZpc{}; font\PYGZhy{}size:medium;\PYGZdq{}\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}p style=\PYGZdq{}line\PYGZhy{}height:180\PYGZpc{}; font\PYGZhy{}size:medium;\PYGZdq{}\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} This is the heart of the notebook. Implement \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}scaled\PYGZus{}dot\PYGZus{}product\PYGZus{}attention(q, k, v, mask=None)\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} following the formula softmax(q k\PYGZlt{}sup\PYGZgt{}T\PYGZlt{}/sup\PYGZgt{} / \PYGZam{}radic;d\PYGZlt{}sub\PYGZgt{}head\PYGZlt{}/sub\PYGZgt{}) v, and implement \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}causal\PYGZus{}mask(T)\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} that returns a lower\PYGZhy{}triangular boolean matrix of shape \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}(T, T)\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}. Read \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}d\PYGZus{}head\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} from the last axis of \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}q\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}, build the scores with a batched matrix multiply against the transpose of \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}k\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}, divide by \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}jnp.sqrt(d\PYGZus{}head)\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}, and when a mask is supplied replace every forbidden score with a large negative number using \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}jnp.where\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} \PYGZlt{}i\PYGZgt{}before\PYGZlt{}/i\PYGZgt{} the softmax. Return both the output and the attention weights so we can plot them. You may use \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}jax.nn.softmax\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} here for the final normalization.}
