\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} Let us prove the scaling argument from the learning note with a quick experiment. For several head dimensions we draw many random query/key pairs, then measure the variance of the raw dot product \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}q\PYGZam{}middot;k\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} and of the scaled dot product \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}q\PYGZam{}middot;k / \PYGZam{}radic;d\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}. The raw variance should grow roughly linearly with \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}d\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}, while the scaled variance should stay close to one regardless of \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}d\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}, which is exactly why the softmax stays well\PYGZhy{}behaved.}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}/p\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}/p\PYGZgt{}}

