\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} \PYGZlt{}p style=\PYGZdq{}line\PYGZhy{}height:180\PYGZpc{}; font\PYGZhy{}size:medium;\PYGZdq{}\PYGZgt{}}
\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} Implement \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}positional\PYGZus{}encoding(T, d)\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} returning a \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}(T, d)\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} array. Build a column vector of positions \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}pos\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} and a row vector of dimension indices \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}i\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}, form \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}angle\PYGZus{}rates = 1 / 10000\PYGZlt{}sup\PYGZgt{}(2(i // 2) / d)\PYGZlt{}/sup\PYGZgt{}\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}, multiply to get the per\PYGZhy{}position angles, and finally select \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}sin\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} for even \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}i\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} and \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}cos\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} for odd \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}i\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} with \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}jnp.where\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{}. Do not loop over positions; use broadcasting so the same code runs on any length.}
