\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} A useful diagnostic is the \PYGZlt{}b\PYGZgt{}entropy\PYGZlt{}/b\PYGZgt{} of each query\PYGZsq{}s attention distribution. A high entropy means the query spreads its attention over many keys, while a low entropy means it concentrates on a few. Under a causal mask the very first query can only attend to one key, so its entropy must be zero, and later queries have more keys available and therefore the room for higher entropy. We plot the entropy of each row of the attention matrix from the snippet above.}
