\PYG{c+c1}{\PYGZsh{} How far back does each position tend to look? For every query we compute the \PYGZlt{}b\PYGZgt{}average attention distance\PYGZlt{}/b\PYGZgt{}, the mean gap \PYGZlt{}code\PYGZgt{}i \PYGZhy{} j\PYGZlt{}/code\PYGZgt{} between the query position \PYGZlt{}i\PYGZgt{}i\PYGZlt{}/i\PYGZgt{} and the key positions \PYGZlt{}i\PYGZgt{}j\PYGZlt{}/i\PYGZgt{}, weighted by the attention it places on each key. With random untrained weights this curve is mostly a function of how many keys are available, but the same plot on a trained model reveals whether heads specialize into looking nearby or far away. To make the trend smoother we average over a longer random sequence.}
